1:["$","main",null,{"className":"site article-page","children":["$","div",null,{"className":"article-frame","children":[["$","a",null,{"className":"desktop-brand","href":"/","children":["$","span",null,{"className":"letter-cascade is-in","aria-label":"Thinkinghaus","children":[["$","b","T-0",{"aria-hidden":"true","style":{"--letter-cascade-index":0},"children":"T"}],["$","b","h-1",{"aria-hidden":"true","style":{"--letter-cascade-index":1},"children":"h"}],["$","b","i-2",{"aria-hidden":"true","style":{"--letter-cascade-index":2},"children":"i"}],["$","b","n-3",{"aria-hidden":"true","style":{"--letter-cascade-index":3},"children":"n"}],["$","b","k-4",{"aria-hidden":"true","style":{"--letter-cascade-index":4},"children":"k"}],["$","b","i-5",{"aria-hidden":"true","style":{"--letter-cascade-index":5},"children":"i"}],["$","b","n-6",{"aria-hidden":"true","style":{"--letter-cascade-index":6},"children":"n"}],["$","b","g-7",{"aria-hidden":"true","style":{"--letter-cascade-index":7},"children":"g"}],["$","b","h-8",{"aria-hidden":"true","style":{"--letter-cascade-index":8},"children":"h"}],["$","b","a-9",{"aria-hidden":"true","style":{"--letter-cascade-index":9},"children":"a"}],["$","b","u-10",{"aria-hidden":"true","style":{"--letter-cascade-index":10},"children":"u"}],["$","b","s-11",{"aria-hidden":"true","style":{"--letter-cascade-index":11},"children":"s"}]]}]}],["$","article",null,{"className":"article-column","children":[["$","header",null,{"className":"article-header","children":[["$","h1",null,{"children":"Corrigible"}],["$","p",null,{"children":"August 10, 2026"}],["$","p",null,{"children":"7 minutes"}]]}],["$","div",null,{"className":"article-body","children":[[["$","p","0-I’ve carried the word *incorrigible* around for years.",{"children":["I’ve carried the word ",["$","em","1",{"children":["incorrigible"]}]," around for years."]}],["$","p","1-I first remember hearing it in the Babe Ruth biopic with John Goodman. Ruth is a kid at St. Mary’s Industrial School, and somewhere in that story he gets branded with this terrible word. I don’t remember the scene precisely anymore, which is probably appropriate: the movie has mostly disappeared from my memory while the label survived. The historical version is bad enough. Ruth’s parents [petitioned the courts to declare their seven-year-old son “incorrigible”](https://sabr.org/bioproj/person/babe-ruth/) before sending him to St. Mary’s.",{"children":["I first remember hearing it in the Babe Ruth biopic with John Goodman. Ruth is a kid at St. Mary’s Industrial School, and somewhere in that story he gets branded with this terrible word. I don’t remember the scene precisely anymore, which is probably appropriate: the movie has mostly disappeared from my memory while the label survived. The historical version is bad enough. Ruth’s parents ",["$","a","1",{"href":"https://sabr.org/bioproj/person/babe-ruth/","rel":"noreferrer","children":["petitioned the courts to declare their seven-year-old son “incorrigible”"]}]," before sending him to St. Mary’s."]}],["$","p","2-There are much worse things you can call a child, but there is something unusually final about *incorrigible*. Difficult describes what is happening. Disobedient describes behavior. Incorrigible reaches forward in time. It says the correction has already failed.",{"children":["There are much worse things you can call a child, but there is something unusually final about ",["$","em","1",{"children":["incorrigible"]}],". Difficult describes what is happening. Disobedient describes behavior. Incorrigible reaches forward in time. It says the correction has already failed."]}],["$","p","3-I know why the word stuck. I have a reactive streak. I can move too quickly from feeling challenged to feeling attacked, especially with people close to me. I don’t particularly enjoy admitting it. It’s easier to recognize that kind of machinery in somebody else than to discover some of the same parts under your own hood.",{"children":"$La"}],"$Lb","$Lc","$Ld","$Le","$Lf","$L10","$L11","$L12","$L13","$L14","$L15","$L16","$L17","$L18","$L19","$L1a","$L1b","$L1c","$L1d","$L1e","$L1f","$L20","$L21"],null]}],"$L22"]}]]}]}]
a:["I know why the word stuck. I have a reactive streak. I can move too quickly from feeling challenged to feeling attacked, especially with people close to me. I don’t particularly enjoy admitting it. It’s easier to recognize that kind of machinery in somebody else than to discover some of the same parts under your own hood."]
b:["$","p","4-The reaction usually contains some information: someone may actually be challenging me, misunderstanding me, dismissing something I care about. The problem is that one true note can become the whole song. Challenge becomes attack. Disagreement becomes threat. The alarm isn’t imaginary; it’s just set a little too sensitive. A smoke detector that goes off every time you make toast is technically doing its job, but it still makes breakfast exhausting.",{"children":["The reaction usually contains some information: someone may actually be challenging me, misunderstanding me, dismissing something I care about. The problem is that one true note can become the whole song. Challenge becomes attack. Disagreement becomes threat. The alarm isn’t imaginary; it’s just set a little too sensitive. A smoke detector that goes off every time you make toast is technically doing its job, but it still makes breakfast exhausting."]}]
c:["$","p","5-I’ve spent years trying to create a little more room between those things. Not to become someone who never gets angry, or to replace intuition with a committee meeting inside my skull. I want more notes on the piano: curiosity, humor, firmness, patience, confusion, even anger when anger is actually called for. When I manage it, it doesn’t feel much like self-control. It feels like I’m more in tune with the world.",{"children":["I’ve spent years trying to create a little more room between those things. Not to become someone who never gets angry, or to replace intuition with a committee meeting inside my skull. I want more notes on the piano: curiosity, humor, firmness, patience, confusion, even anger when anger is actually called for. When I manage it, it doesn’t feel much like self-control. It feels like I’m more in tune with the world."]}]
d:["$","p","6-Other people’s experience of the old pattern can still be fair. They encountered the behavior, not my intentions about improving it. But there’s a difference between saying *this is a persistent pattern* and *this is what you are*. One describes accumulated evidence. The other quietly turns the evidence into a prediction about the future.",{"children":["Other people’s experience of the old pattern can still be fair. They encountered the behavior, not my intentions about improving it. But there’s a difference between saying ",["$","em","1",{"children":["this is a persistent pattern"]}]," and ",["$","em","3",{"children":["this is what you are"]}],". One describes accumulated evidence. The other quietly turns the evidence into a prediction about the future."]}]
e:["$","p","7-We need predictions. We couldn’t operate without categories. I need to be able to say *tree* without approaching every oak as though botany had just been invented that morning. Experience teaches pattern recognition. Intuition gets better. Sometimes I meet someone and think I know the type and, unfortunately, I do.",{"children":["We need predictions. We couldn’t operate without categories. I need to be able to say ",["$","em","1",{"children":["tree"]}]," without approaching every oak as though botany had just been invented that morning. Experience teaches pattern recognition. Intuition gets better. Sometimes I meet someone and think I know the type and, unfortunately, I do."]}]
f:["$","p","8-The problem isn’t categorization. It’s forgetting that the category is compression.",{"children":["The problem isn’t categorization. It’s forgetting that the category is compression."]}]
10:["$","p","9-I used to have fairly fixed ideas about conservatives and military culture. Then I lived in Washington, D.C., very close to the Pentagon, surrounded by thoughtful, kind, family-oriented people whom I respected and connected with. My politics didn’t suddenly disappear. Something more useful happened: the category stopped being able to contain the people. Up close, the abstraction had to compete with actual things.",{"children":["I used to have fairly fixed ideas about conservatives and military culture. Then I lived in Washington, D.C., very close to the Pentagon, surrounded by thoughtful, kind, family-oriented people whom I respected and connected with. My politics didn’t suddenly disappear. Something more useful happened: the category stopped being able to contain the people. Up close, the abstraction had to compete with actual things."]}]
11:["$","p","10-There’s a much more extreme version of this in [*Accidental Courtesy*](https://www.pbs.org/independentlens/documentaries/accidental-courtesy/), about Black musician Daryl Davis befriending Klansmen and eventually winding up with some of their robes.",{"children":["There’s a much more extreme version of this in ",["$","a","1",{"href":"https://www.pbs.org/independentlens/documentaries/accidental-courtesy/","rel":"noreferrer","children":[["$","em","0",{"children":["Accidental Courtesy"]}]]}],", about Black musician Daryl Davis befriending Klansmen and eventually winding up with some of their robes."]}]
12:["$","p","11-[A short essay on Bear Blog about philosophical melancholy](https://xtoblog.bearblog.dev/the-inevitable-loneliness-we-must-suffer/) led me to [a passage from David Hume](https://davidhume.org/texts/t/1/4/7) that feels like the same idea wearing eighteenth-century clothes.",{"children":[["$","a","0",{"href":"https://xtoblog.bearblog.dev/the-inevitable-loneliness-we-must-suffer/","rel":"noreferrer","children":["A short essay on Bear Blog about philosophical melancholy"]}]," led me to ",["$","a","2",{"href":"https://davidhume.org/texts/t/1/4/7","rel":"noreferrer","children":["a passage from David Hume"]}]," that feels like the same idea wearing eighteenth-century clothes."]}]
13:["$","p","12-Hume has reasoned himself into a hole. His thoughts about human nature have become so consuming that reason itself can’t get him back out. His solution is magnificently undignified: “I dine, I play a game of back-gammon,” talk with friends, have a good time. A few hours later he returns to his grand speculations and finds them cold, strained, and faintly ridiculous.",{"children":["Hume has reasoned himself into a hole. His thoughts about human nature have become so consuming that reason itself can’t get him back out. His solution is magnificently undignified: “I dine, I play a game of back-gammon,” talk with friends, have a good time. A few hours later he returns to his grand speculations and finds them cold, strained, and faintly ridiculous."]}]
14:["$","p","13-I don’t read this as a vacation from thinking. Dinner and backgammon are doing epistemological work. Hume changes the conditions of the experiment. He lets sensation, play and other people back into the room. The philosophical problem hasn’t been disproved; its proportions have changed because reality has been allowed to vote again.",{"children":["I don’t read this as a vacation from thinking. Dinner and backgammon are doing epistemological work. Hume changes the conditions of the experiment. He lets sensation, play and other people back into the room. The philosophical problem hasn’t been disproved; its proportions have changed because reality has been allowed to vote again."]}]
15:["$","p","14-I’ve felt a version of this in monasteries. I’ve spent long stretches living in one, and a monastery can teach real things about interdependence, attention and community. But it is also a laboratory. The conditions have been arranged to make certain things easier to see. Coming home doesn’t invalidate what happened there. It removes the controls. Maintaining a Zen attitude around people who did not enroll in your spiritual experiment turns out to be a different curriculum.",{"children":["I’ve felt a version of this in monasteries. I’ve spent long stretches living in one, and a monastery can teach real things about interdependence, attention and community. But it is also a laboratory. The conditions have been arranged to make certain things easier to see. Coming home doesn’t invalidate what happened there. It removes the controls. Maintaining a Zen attitude around people who did not enroll in your spiritual experiment turns out to be a different curriculum."]}]
16:["$","p","15-Some truths become visible under controlled conditions. Others only appear when the controls come off, and the same seems to be true of ourselves.",{"children":["Some truths become visible under controlled conditions. Others only appear when the controls come off, and the same seems to be true of ourselves."]}]
17:["$","p","16-The Buddhist dialogue [*The Questions of King Milinda*](https://suttacentral.net/mil3.2.1/en/tw_rhysdavids) contains an exchange I keep coming back to. King Milinda asks Nāgasena whether a person who continues through time is the same person or another.",{"children":["The Buddhist dialogue ",["$","a","1",{"href":"https://suttacentral.net/mil3.2.1/en/tw_rhysdavids","rel":"noreferrer","children":[["$","em","0",{"children":["The Questions of King Milinda"]}]]}]," contains an exchange I keep coming back to. King Milinda asks Nāgasena whether a person who continues through time is the same person or another."]}]
18:["$","p","17-“Neither the same nor another.”",{"children":["“Neither the same nor another.”"]}]
19:["$","p","18-That lands closer to my experience than either alternative. I am not a fresh character spawning each morning with the save file deleted. I inherit habits, consequences, relationships, a nervous system, and all the little channels I’ve spent decades cutting into the earth. Karma has momentum, but momentum isn’t destiny.",{"children":["That lands closer to my experience than either alternative. I am not a fresh character spawning each morning with the save file deleted. I inherit habits, consequences, relationships, a nervous system, and all the little channels I’ve spent decades cutting into the earth. Karma has momentum, but momentum isn’t destiny."]}]
1a:["$","p","19-I can move a rock today. Sometimes that changes the current noticeably. Sometimes I move the same damn rock for six months. Sometimes I lose my footing and discover that the old channel is doing perfectly well without my cooperation.",{"children":["I can move a rock today. Sometimes that changes the current noticeably. Sometimes I move the same damn rock for six months. Sometimes I lose my footing and discover that the old channel is doing perfectly well without my cooperation."]}]
1b:["$","p","20-If I’ve flooded somebody’s house, I don’t get to stand upstream pointing proudly at the rocks I’ve been moving. Their landscape contains what happened. They don’t owe me immediate trust in the new channel.",{"children":["If I’ve flooded somebody’s house, I don’t get to stand upstream pointing proudly at the rocks I’ve been moving. Their landscape contains what happened. They don’t owe me immediate trust in the new channel."]}]
1c:["$","p","21-There’s another Buddhist image, [the story of the two arrows](https://suttacentral.net/sn36.6/en/sujato), that I find useful even though I’m borrowing it fairly loosely. The first arrow is the pain that actually happens. The second is the suffering we add to it.",{"children":["There’s another Buddhist image, ",["$","a","1",{"href":"https://suttacentral.net/sn36.6/en/sujato","rel":"noreferrer","children":["the story of the two arrows"]}],", that I find useful even though I’m borrowing it fairly loosely. The first arrow is the pain that actually happens. The second is the suffering we add to it."]}]
1d:["$","p","22-Sometimes the first arrow is mine to own: I reacted badly. I made things worse. There are consequences. Taking responsibility means not wriggling out of that.",{"children":["Sometimes the first arrow is mine to own: I reacted badly. I made things worse. There are consequences. Taking responsibility means not wriggling out of that."]}]
1e:["$","p","23-The second arrow is deciding that the mistake proves nothing has changed. That this is what I am. That all the rocks I moved upstream were imaginary because the river flooded again.",{"children":["The second arrow is deciding that the mistake proves nothing has changed. That this is what I am. That all the rocks I moved upstream were imaginary because the river flooded again."]}]
1f:["$","p","24-I don’t want a philosophy that tells me my first impressions are worthless, that categories are evil, that judgment is unenlightened, or that everybody becomes wonderful once we understand them properly. Sometimes the closer look confirms exactly what I feared.",{"children":["I don’t want a philosophy that tells me my first impressions are worthless, that categories are evil, that judgment is unenlightened, or that everybody becomes wonderful once we understand them properly. Sometimes the closer look confirms exactly what I feared."]}]
20:["$","p","25-I want my understanding to remain corrigible. Close enough to people, including myself, that new information can still get in. Responsible for where the river has been without pretending it has stopped moving.",{"children":["I want my understanding to remain corrigible. Close enough to people, including myself, that new information can still get in. Responsible for where the river has been without pretending it has stopped moving."]}]
21:["$","p","26-I still hate the word *incorrigible*.",{"children":["I still hate the word ",["$","em","1",{"children":["incorrigible"]}],"."]}]
22:["$","footer",null,{"className":"footer","children":[["$","a",null,{"className":"footer-brand","href":"/","children":"Thinkinghaus"}],["$","nav",null,{"className":"footer-links","aria-label":"Site","children":[["$","a",null,{"href":"/about.html","children":"About"}],["$","a",null,{"href":"/links.html","children":"Links"}],["$","a",null,{"href":"https://trackinghaus-alpha.vercel.app","children":"Stats"}],["$","a",null,{"href":"/rss.xml","type":"application/rss+xml","children":"RSS"}]]}]]}]
